course: dictionary
lesson: 12439
title: Working out a hidden meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To decipher something means to work out what it says when it is hard to understand at first. It is often a secret code, very messy handwriting, or an old language. «The spy finally deciphered the secret message.» The message looked like nonsense until she worked out the code.
explain: Deciphered is the past form of decipher. You can also use it for a puzzle that felt confusing: «Mia deciphered the riddle and laughed.» Here it means she understood something puzzling.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like code, secret, message, or hard to read tell you that deciphered is about solving something. Then swap in your meaning: "worked out" should still make sense in the sentence.
fact: Decipher means to work out the meaning of something that is hard to read or understand.
fact: «Deciphered» means worked out, or turned into plain words.
fact: Code-breakers in wartime deciphered secret messages.
fact: Egyptian hieroglyphs were deciphered with help from the Rosetta Stone.
fact: In a simple code, each letter might be moved three places along the alphabet, so you can decipher the message by moving each letter back three places.
exercise: «The spy deciphered the secret message in one night.» What does deciphered mean here? | Wrote a long letter | Lost the message | *Worked out the meaning of a secret code | Sent it by post
exercise: «The faded writing could hardly be deciphered.» What does this suggest? | It was printed in large, clear letters | *It was very hard to read | It was read aloud at school | It was written in gold ink
exercise: «Mia deciphered the riddle and laughed.» Find and copy the one word that means worked out. | laughed | *deciphered | riddle | Mia
test: «The detective deciphered the note, which was written in a secret code.» What did the detective do to the note? | Lost it on the bus | Put it in the bin | Folded it into a paper plane | *Worked out what the secret code said
test: Which word could replace deciphered in «The team deciphered the clues»? | forgot | painted | ate | *worked out
exam: «Sam could not read the old map at first, but he deciphered it at last.» What does deciphered mean? | Hid | Tore up | *Worked out the meaning of | Gave up on
